<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Italy's biggest-ever wine heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0329e429d11c0f9d992216937a6d1ee83b2f18818b60260e00316e5a4cb6a5d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:02:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist--5d4a20ca2b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist" /><summary type="html">A multi million euro wine heist in Italy. As thieves in Tuscany steal 30 thousand bottles of the one of the most iconic labels in the country from a warehouse of the the prized Marchesi Antinori winery as it prepared for a major export. The company said in the past few hours, they believe two vans and up to six thieves were involved. Gavin Lee speaks to France 24's correspondent in Rome, Seema Gupta.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump strikes diesel deal with Putin, reversing years of pressure on Russia over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:048b18356b7d348ea986c4427b3c3a4f31697fd00c55ccbbd596e846aab942e9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:02:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:00:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war--81c65c075c6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that Russia had agreed to immediately supply more than 300,000 tonnes of diesel to US and global markets in an effort to cut fuel prices before November's midterm elections. The move marks a stunning change of policy after the US and its allies hit Russia with waves of sanctions over its invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris court jails Indian man for leading sadist neo-Nazi cult that tortured girls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36d82c8ab5cb5e4107755bf2a3d9ba859d3d7da07ee65df34deed323fd69217b</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:02:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T19:45:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-paris-court-jails-indian-man-for-leading-sadist-neo-nazi-cult-that-tortured-girls--2e156af0653d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-paris-court-jails-indian-man-for-leading-sadist-neo-nazi-cult-that-tortured-girls" /><summary type="html">A 29-year-old Indian man was sentenced to 20 years in prison Friday in a Paris trial over his alleged involvement in an international criminal network that targeted vulnerable children in the US, Britain and Canada and coerced them into producing violent and sexual videos.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Powerful 7.6 magnitude quake shakes Panama, triggering tsunami warning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:587c44c58e8ae58003285c2504394036be8a3320d94662eae937f7641e3b0d11</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:02:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T18:41:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning--2b8cfe163ef0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful 7.6 magnitude quake shakes Panama, triggering tsunami warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b10c4d6cf03704a418bce7c75d2bd69b247b4b9e8a1f8a2090f7a1e0e758ffb</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:02:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T18:39:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning--2b8cfe163ef0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261009-powerful-7-6-magnitude-quake-shakes-panama-triggering-tsunami-warning" /><summary type="html">A strong 7.6 magnitude earthquake struck near the southern ​coast ‌of Panama ⁠on Friday at a 10 km depth, ‌according to the US Geological ⁠Survey, shaking buildings as far away as the capital and prompting evacuations. The US Tsunami Warning ​System showed potential tsunami threats across much of Central America's Pacific ​coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France Protests, Israel's 'politically charged' remembrance, Ethopia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00cfef33b652809a3ec7612977cf2ccf0f51104164b9a6e6b388f8d7977327a1</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T18:28:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261009-france-protests-israel-s-politically-charged-remembrance-ethopia-ukraine--45fe531857a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261009-france-protests-israel-s-politically-charged-remembrance-ethopia-ukraine" /><summary type="html">It’s been a week of vigils, protests and political upheaval – from Israel, where three years after the Hamas-led attacks, former hostages and mourners called for accountability over the failures of October 7th, as questions grow over the stalled path to peace in Gaza; to France, where mass demonstrations over chronic underfunding and poor conditions have drawn students, unions and hundreds of thousands of protesters into the streets, just months ahead of a presidential election. In Spain, Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has made the housing crisis the centrepiece of a high-stakes electoral gamble, as protests intensify following the death of a pensioner whose eviction helped ignite the movement. And in the UK, questions remain over a suspected Iranian plot targeting US aircraft at RAF Fairford, after American B-1 bombers were hastily withdrawn amid warnings of a serious and immediate threat.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Navi Pillay awarded Peace Prize: 'Lifetime spent fighting for what's right &amp; to uphold human rights'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a765443e9745294c75f1b6b7e2f983c5650d7c16998cb5cc79b03661ab1ac1ab</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:27:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-awarded-peace-prize-lifetime-spent-fighting-for-what-s-right-to-uphold-human-rights--7321e527061c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/navi-pillay-awarded-peace-prize-lifetime-spent-fighting-for-what-s-right-to-uphold-human-rights" /><summary type="html">Haxie Meyers-Belkin is pleased to welcome Rosa Freedman, Professor of Law Conflict and Global Development at the University of Reading. Navi Pillay's career represents a remarkable contribution to international law and human rights, from her pioneering role in post-apartheid South Africa to her work at the United Nations. Yet her legacy also raises difficult questions about political impartiality, particularly in relation to Israel and Gaza. She believes we need to distinguish between the significance of her lifelong achievements and the controversy surrounding the decision to award her the Nobel Peace Prize at this particular moment. More broadly, this debate invites us to examine whether the prize is recognising individual merit or increasingly serving as a vehicle for political messaging. At a time when international law and multilateral institutions face mounting pressure, and serious threats, Freedman asserts that the challenge is to scrutinise their shortcomings without undermining the principles they exist to uphold.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 FlyDubai co-pilot planned suicide attack on Tel Aviv airport, inspired by 9/11, UAE prosecutor says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d9f9414c83181630b280ef8aac92064280c1588f6f691c42bab0aeab1112b0c</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:09:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11--e457237ce44f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11" /></entry><entry><title>FlyDubai co-pilot planned suicide attack on Tel Aviv airport, inspired by 9/11, prosecutor says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc337cec5d43c1dc402e336f96f6a86d33faf777dd61b530ce3c59446c8479f</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:04:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11--e457237ce44f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot who attacked the captain of FlyDubai flight 1073 had planned to crash the plane into Tel Aviv's international airport in a suicide attack, the United Arab Emirates' top prosecutor said Friday. The Israel-bound flight carrying 182 people made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Unweaving Jeffrey Epstein’s web: What the files have revealed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3685d560e48fe7ff671b799e4b70cccb8ca8f9bf9abca8f31dc34735039268f</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T17:00:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed--84e88b833ace.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-unweaving-jeffrey-epstein-s-web-what-the-files-have-revealed" /><summary type="html">On January 30, 2026, the US Justice Department released 3 million documents. Photos, videos, emails, text messages, court records... All connected to one man: Jeffrey Epstein. Since then, media outlets around the world have brought to light the vast amount of people that appear in the Epstein files. Eight months on, what what do these revelations tell us about Jeffrey Epstein’s network? How did it operate? FRANCE 24 journalist Ava Luquet spent months digging through the files. In this video, she takes a closer look at what they reveal about the predator’s network and its inner workings.</summary></entry><entry><title>Le Pen's top ally Bardella faces fresh claims he sought to cover up past anti-Semitic comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e226a589b2f69ed000ff79c1dacf4e818a19c9664a5639cb2042a7a07ba3e19</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:53:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-le-pen-top-ally-bardella-faces-fresh-claims-he-sought-to-cover-up-past-anti-semitic-comment--e1866b154c72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-le-pen-top-ally-bardella-faces-fresh-claims-he-sought-to-cover-up-past-anti-semitic-comments" /><summary type="html">France's far-right National Rally leader Jordan Bardella deleted data from a former activist Facebook account as soon as allegations surfaced that he wrote anti-Semitic comments in his youth, French investigative weekly Le Canard enchaîné said Friday, piling pressure on the top ally of presidential frontrunner Marine Le Pen.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Covid recovery fund was 'absolutely a success': European Court of Auditors' Pierre Moscovici</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b8752b288c482afdcdb1ae58f3cb504f166a5676621d056e4fb42b7a6076618</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:51:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovi--05c75909711a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovici" /><summary type="html">2020 was an annus horribilis. Covid stalked the land. Lockdowns, curfews and social distancing were the order of the day. But there was a silver lining: European countries showed themselves to be capable of great solidarity, jointly procuring vaccines and then agreeing on a mammoth post-Covid recovery fund, the Recovery and Resilience Facility (RRF). That fund has disbursed €450 billion in grants and loans to EU member states since 2021. As the RRF enters its crucial final phase, we take stock of the situation with Pierre Moscovici, the French member of the European Court of Auditors (ECA).</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Nobel Peace Prize: Who is Navanethem “Navi” Pillay?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62fdce4260ad54b49f2f7688cbb17ed43847d20eb51c17b7e5eef7ee81987229</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:47:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-2026-nobel-peace-prize-who-is-navanethem-navi-pillay--b0da69c0edf8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-2026-nobel-peace-prize-who-is-navanethem-navi-pillay" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to South African Navanethem “Navi” Pillay on Friday, October 9, 2026. The 85-year-old South Africa-born served as United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights and chair of the Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territories.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students vow to keep up protests as UN voices 'concern' over violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2395c6e37204c61347781099f7784dc9b9bce6dce9d04552cd65a46b9abd7f1</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protests-as-un-voices-concern-over-violence--49c7734d8ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protests-as-un-voices-concern-over-violence" /><summary type="html">French student unions ​vowed on Friday to keep up the fight even as the government registered a "marked slowdown" in a protest movement that has rattled the country for over a week. The UN human rights agency called for de-escalation, voicing concern over violent clashes with police that have caused severe injuries among teenage protesters.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>2027 spring-summer ready-to-wear collections: Audacity, movement and sensuality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af8dc6edb44e352310750962c8d272737d00b2fd8efb896a61d5c7fb06ec87c5</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:26:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/fashion/20261009-2027-spring-summer-ready-to-wear-collections-audacity-movement-and-sensuality--9894419402b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/fashion/20261009-2027-spring-summer-ready-to-wear-collections-audacity-movement-and-sensuality" /><summary type="html">We bring you all the latest from Paris Fashion Week. For Weinsanto, audacity is about finding a lightness, as embodied by the LGBTQ+ community. At Issey Miyake, it's about sensuality rooted in the Japanese concept of Ma, the space that bridges the gap between fabric and skin. It's a similar story at Yohji Yamamoto who, at 83, is still on the hunt for emotions.</summary><category term="Fashion" /></entry><entry><title>Israel a rare dissenting voice as praise pours in for Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5143bd3c21d3943c96e552dfa53170588a6547a9d9587890ca350968c834f50d</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:20:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay--0ac82efe71b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay" /><summary type="html">Advocates of human rights and international justice cheered, even as Israeli officials fumed, after South African jurist and former UN human rights chief Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday. The 85-year-old drew wide praise for decades of work, including investigating crimes in Rwanda, Israel and the occupied Palestinian territories.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Criminal Court faces 'test of resilience' as US imposes sweeping sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2a0699dc8777ce8f142da515a82f4a83a3e1ff388b826abb1f0e7d50e8ccc9a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions--8a8a0bb4e4e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has imposed sweeping new sanctions on the International Criminal Court as part of its campaign to dismantle what it describes as a "rogue" tribunal, threatening to cripple its operations. Following the move, ⁠the European Union said it was "ready to take any necessary measures to enable the court to carry out its work".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Falling test scores in schools startle EU countries: Why are standards going down?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd0fbc6893cfabb96d9256bd69548558acf0f294a5a8a0465239590d3f53fde9</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:03:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-falling-test-scores-in-schools-startle-eu-countries-why-are-standards-going-down--52f4dba6ca3b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-falling-test-scores-in-schools-startle-eu-countries-why-are-standards-going-down" /><summary type="html">It has been dubbed "the PISA shock". Countries that had been used to their school pupils performing well in test scores are seeing a plunge in standards. The PISA test is an international assessment led by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), which measures how well 15‑year‑olds in over 80 countries apply reading, mathematics and science skills to real‑world problems. In the latest rankings, France's results were the worst it has ever had, and Germany's school pupils got their worst PISA report card too.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Four astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4f4084af521b24214d08f02b1789ca32167451dd17691681924f319af8a8792</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:43:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-four-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space--90d38341d6be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-four-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space" /><summary type="html">An astronaut crew that carried out an eight-month mission aboard the International Space Station splashed down as planned Thursday off the coast of California. During the mission, Sophie Adenot became the first French female astronaut to venture outside the space station for a spacewalk. In all, she undertook three spacewalks on August 18 and 25, and September 1.</summary></entry><entry><title>Callum Turner's new film sparkles at Dinard Film Festival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5a2cfc6bea0fd4e3e4d8ac5e040efe71ba1eec356f75756b392935279cc9c2</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:34:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261009-callum-turner-s-new-film-sparkles-at-dinard-film-festival--b230e2d48881.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261009-callum-turner-s-new-film-sparkles-at-dinard-film-festival" /><summary type="html">British and Irish cinema have been in the spotlight at the Breton resort of Dinard for more than three decades, with films like "The Full Monty" and "Billy Elliot" getting their starts at the town's annual film festival. FRANCE 24's Culture editor Eve Jackson brings us the latest from this year’s edition, from its line-up to the financial woes that could spell the end of the festival.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Lawsuits blame Fox News for deaths of journalists in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d91b6fef64bcd09cc34b5c665e559e1dfd235da10e74e6220828a40401f235d4</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:23:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine--d976749efeb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop revisits a fatal assignment for a Fox News team in Ukraine. On March 14, 2022, a Russian strike hit the crew reporting near the capital Kyiv. Reporter Benjamin Hall was seriously injured and two other journalists were killed. The journalists' families are suing Fox, saying the network put the story ahead of its people. Our guest is NPR's David Folkenflik.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>'Absolute torture': Female US inmate in critical condition after botched execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c38461b228d93458c0bced0e6ee5d30107dd9afe33fe0e5aef536be9262e466a</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:03:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-absolute-torture-female-us-inmate-in-critical-condition-after-botched-execution--d31d2c36c49e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-absolute-torture-female-us-inmate-in-critical-condition-after-botched-execution" /><summary type="html">A condemned female murderer who survived two lethal injections during a botched execution by the US state of Tennessee was in critical condition and receiving "life-saving care," according to her attorneys. In an extraordinary chain of events, Christa Pike, 50, was whisked from a prison execution chamber to a hospital, still alive despite two deadly doses of pentobarbital. What happened to Pike is "absolute torture," said Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, Spokesperson for Together Against the Death Penalty (ECPM), speaking to FRANCE 24's Alison Sargent.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sierra Leone: From 'blood diamonds' to stones of hope?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea6be6da567f2dfd85f574436bf6aa7de2415d611041b3579e50787cae5af958</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:58:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen--522d29c385dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen" /><summary type="html">"Blood diamonds" became infamous for funding the brutal civil war in Sierra Leone. Beginning 25 years ago, the Kimberley Process aimed to put an end to this illegal trade. Accused of complicity in the conflict, the diamond industry has since sought to clean up its image, emphasising an ethical shift. But a quarter of a century on, have the former "blood diamonds" truly become synonymous with development? FRANCE 24's Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Russia says all clear after contact tracing in reported plague case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffcb6405e81eed26c87911b10c41b1b01491415bad660ed91352558d4b675b12</id><updated>2026-10-09T21:03:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:53:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-russia-says-all-clear-after-contact-tracing-in-reported-plague-case--38ca4089af70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-russia-says-all-clear-after-contact-tracing-in-reported-plague-case" /><summary type="html">Russia has detected no health issues or dangerous micro-organisms after tracing all contacts of a woman who reportedly died of plague, the governor of Siberia's Irkutsk region said Thursday. Russia has not confirmed the woman died of plague, and Governor Igor Kobzev said in his statement she had contracted "community-acquired pneumonia".</summary></entry></feed>
